            <ArticleTitle>Anticonvulsant hypersensitivity syndrome secondary to carbamazepine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-96</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anticonvulsant hypersensitivity syndrome (AHS) is a potentially fatal multiorgan drug reaction that presents with various cutaneous eruptions. There is a genetic predisposition to such reactions. We present a young woman with AHS due to carbamazepine that presented as an atypical erythema multiforme with elevated liver enzymes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
